{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_8559396a59c34645883cfd92b96d9ab9a228d3c551116f6ea4f5d3388acb0cdc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Runtime dependencies include jina 3.15.1.dev14, openai>=0.27.5, langchain 0.0.153, streamlit 1.9.0, jcloud, jina-hubble-sdk, click, psutil, and pinned pydantic/typing packages."}],"claim_ids":["clm_8559396a59c34645883cfd92b96d9ab9a228d3c551116f6ea4f5d3388acb0cdc"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_c19434b5c5f2462ead59f82c49eaa930","id":"pg_98df30f10230597db17f3ead835c1c6a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/jina-ai-dev-gpt-requirements-txt-f6c151f93b02-3ead835c1c6a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_728a35f58ebc52788d26b1b3b9f996ad"],"title":"jina-ai/dev-gpt/requirements.txt @ f6c151f93b02","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c19434b5c5f2462ead59f82c49eaa930"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_00896d16911fa13278a20a73a998cf876e35e0d609573e3e072e59d46c78dba0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Dev-GPT is a CLI tool with subcommands including generate, run, deploy, and configure, invoked as 'dev-gpt <command>' with flags like --description, --model, and --path."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0cc6a55a8446676b17aff36c276c71afda1ac001ec0d598273c945b93635f797"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented cost and time bounds: generation takes about 5–15 minutes and costs roughly $0.50–$3.00 per microservice on GPT-4 or $0.05–$0.30 on GPT-3.5-turbo."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f5d7ef2d0ea6424c4bf23b0bef8e4debbef750a5ecb4f2fe813ac7f6629f93c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is framed as a virtual three-role team — Product Manager, Developer, and DevOps — that builds microservices from a natural-language description."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6db79062a171a2c4beeb8a509cd7728288648e8b2390173c24d6c8a35cd9f62d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are invited to open PRs or issues, and a checklist of next steps and nice-to-haves (e.g. verifying Windows/Linux support, adding tests, cleaning up duplicate code) is maintained in the README."},{"claim_ids":["clm_812e7cda94851aa9114e2ecc72cbc6b206da2fe6bde4a5ea226edf4a0a98e34c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"After a successful build the tool pushes the Docker image to a registry, deploys the microservice, and generates a Streamlit playground for testing it in the browser."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ec997263490fac80df01d97630b5606cd6420398616fa52a91140365d325001"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Generation works by proposing multiple implementation strategies, generating code plus tests and a Dockerfile per strategy, building the image, and using build error messages to retry; after 10 consecutive failures it moves to the next strategy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ad205eb121e6f371542b12f04732a09cc7950edbb017482e3ec9e37a77ad618c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The model choice is user-selectable between gpt-3.5-turbo and gpt-4, with gpt-3.5-turbo described as roughly 10x cheaper but less capable of complex microservices; default is the largest model the key can access."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d94335e85be3acf3c95ae3352c62319c54e8110b39a88dda20e55d18626f2861"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product requires an OpenAI API key with gpt-4 access (gpt-3.5-turbo also accepted for generation), and optionally GOOGLE_API_KEY and GOOGLE_CSE_ID to enable web-content search."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e651c96b6ac8f9f80baa4703aafe8633dbcc081752a76433e266879463f0686d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"For each strategy the generator produces microservice.py, test_microservice.py, requirements.txt, and a Dockerfile whose build also runs the tests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f56a3beb137933338722346b9f8dae0ec26e14a498605017c10d6c9dbcbabb96"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README marks the project as an experimental version, and notes a known bug where code generation can hang forever, requiring aborting and redoing the generation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_00896d16911fa13278a20a73a998cf876e35e0d609573e3e072e59d46c78dba0","clm_0cc6a55a8446676b17aff36c276c71afda1ac001ec0d598273c945b93635f797","clm_3f5d7ef2d0ea6424c4bf23b0bef8e4debbef750a5ecb4f2fe813ac7f6629f93c","clm_6db79062a171a2c4beeb8a509cd7728288648e8b2390173c24d6c8a35cd9f62d","clm_812e7cda94851aa9114e2ecc72cbc6b206da2fe6bde4a5ea226edf4a0a98e34c","clm_8ec997263490fac80df01d97630b5606cd6420398616fa52a91140365d325001","clm_ad205eb121e6f371542b12f04732a09cc7950edbb017482e3ec9e37a77ad618c","clm_d94335e85be3acf3c95ae3352c62319c54e8110b39a88dda20e55d18626f2861","clm_e651c96b6ac8f9f80baa4703aafe8633dbcc081752a76433e266879463f0686d","clm_f56a3beb137933338722346b9f8dae0ec26e14a498605017c10d6c9dbcbabb96"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_c19434b5c5f2462ead59f82c49eaa930","id":"pg_b4d25c5175145ccfb0e53a279afac327","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":